        "content": "<p>Hi,<br>\nI'm playing around with <code>conv</code> mode, and got an error that seems unexpected:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- panics at Lean.Expr.mvarId!</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- (kernel) application type mismatch [...]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">pattern</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- panics at Lean.Expr.mvarId!</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">lhs</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">pattern</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Diff\"><pre><span></span><code>(kernel) application type mismatch\n<span class=\"w\"> </span> id (congrArg (HAdd.hAdd x) (Eq.trans (Int.sub_self x) (Eq.refl 0)))\nargument has type\n<span class=\"w\"> </span> x + (x - x) = x + 0\nbut function has type\n<span class=\"w\"> </span> x + (x - x) = x → x + (x - x) = x\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The panic seems to be a bug which I reported <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/issues/14055\">here</a>, but I'm wondering whether this difference between <code>Nat</code> and <code>Int</code> is a separate issue, or rather whether it's also a bug or a misuse of <code>conv</code>.</p>",
